From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiritake Kumi <root@niconiconi.us>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:40:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: put the Milk-V Duo 256M USB port in
 device mode

The board has a single Type-C port and no VBUS switch. In host mode nothing can
be plugged into it, while in device mode the board shows up as a USB network
adapter when connected to a computer, which is how the Debian image is reached
without a serial cable.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
index a2797c0bd..b89cde7c0 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
@@ -116,6 +116,6 @@ &uart0 {
 };
 
 &usb {
-	dr_mode = "host";
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
